    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="1040" n="1022" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p1/pg1022"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.5/12–354</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Counselor of the Department of State
                        (MacArthur) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-12-03">December 3, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I attach a draft paper prepared by a State-Defense-CIA working group on
                    activities that could be undertaken by the Manila Pact powers to combat
                    Communist subversion. This paper would be tabled in the Manila Pact working
                    group which will begin operations here in Washington on December 6. Before we
                    actually table the paper in our working group, we will discuss it with the
                    British <pb facs="1041" n="1023" xml:id="pg1023"/> here in compliance with the
                    request which Ambassador Makins made to you last week.</p>
                <p>We are anxious to talk to the British about this as soon as possible but before
                    doing so, I wanted you to glance over the paper and see if there were any points
                    which you wished to make before we go ahead and show it to the British.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d409-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas MacArthur</hi> II<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d409-f2"/></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d409-a1.xml" xpointer="d409-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d409-f1" n="1" xml:id="d409-f1-content">
                <p>This memorandum bears several handwritten marginal notes, including the
                    following: “OK JFD” and “Sec approved R [oderic] O’C [onnor]”. Another note
                    indicates that MacArthur was informed of the Secretary’s action by phone on Dec.
                    3.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d409-f2" n="2" xml:id="d409-f2-content">
                <p>A note in MacArthur’s handwriting underneath his signature reads: “P.S. CIA will
                    have some minor modifications simply for clarification. We now plan to talk to
                    British on next Tuesday, Dec. 7.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
